# Native HTML/JS computer

Words: [README.md — Words used](../../README.md#words-used-in-this-project).
This is **copy 1** of “no dukpy / vendored HTML titles” (copy 2:
[CONSTITUTION.md](../../CONSTITUTION.md) Vendored-titles mandate).

This is a **standalone NLISC-JS** machine (Native Language Instruction Set
Computing — JavaScript **bytecode** is the **ISA** Instruction Set
Architecture; HTML is the title file; no general CSS engine). There is no
hidden CPU, no browser-on-FPGA, no Linux. NLISC-BASIC sibling = method only,
not pins or tokens.

**Forbidden as the machine:** dukpy / Duktape / V8 / QuickJS / Node / Chrome;
Z80 / RISC-V / MicroBlaze / any soft CPU; executing JS **source** as one giant
RTL FSM (bytecode is what the chip fetches).

```
LOAD "NAME.HTML" → RUN
  → V1.0: minted NAME.JSH from card.img → JMR VM
  → PYTHON / FPGA-SIM / BOARD share that image. Chrome = authoring only.
```

**V1.0 disk is `card.img`.** `storage/` is the seed — rebuild with
`make_sd_image.py create`. `LOAD` shows HTML; `RUN` loads the minted `.JSH`.
Compile errors at card create use HTML line numbers. Missing path → loud
`?NH` (tracked debt, never done). ESC is machine BREAK to READY — titles
must not steal it. Do **not** compile `storage/*.HTML` on host `RUN` while
the board plays the card.

**Temp V1.0 (host mint):** compile happens when you **make the
card** — `make_sd_image.py` mints `NAME.JSH` from that HTML. **V1.5 compile
is live:** `LOAD` → `EDIT` → **`COMPILE`** → `RUN`. `RUN` still loads `.JSH`.

**Three rooms:** **BRAM** = dual FB + code + heap (do not shrink for a small
die; ASIC ~30 mm², ~1 MB-class SRAM). **µSD** = disk (`NAME.HTML`; temp
minted `.JSH` until V1.5 `COMPILE`). **External 4 MB SRAM** = ASET art only
(`addr[20:0]`, 16-bit, `we`/`req`/`ack`; FPGA = DDR3 behind that port; SIM =
model behind the same port). No `NAME.DAT`. No
64K BASIC house. Do not pack/downscale/quantize Donkey sheets into code BRAM.

**Files:** `storage/*.HTML` only (card builder may **mint** `.JSH` onto the
µSD; do not keep `.JSH` in `storage/`). `storage/games_*` = upstream, not
DIR/card. `NAME.JS` is not a twin of `NAME.HTML`. Order of rungs:
`python-first-parity`. FPGA-SIM default: `never-fake-fpga-sim`.
